{
  "title": "76: al-Insaan الانسان",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nهَلْ اَتٰى عَلَى الْاِنْسَانِ حِيْنٌ مِّنَ الدَّهْرِ لَمْ يَكُنْ شَيْئًا مَّذْكُوْرًا‏(1)\nHAL ATAA A’LAL INSAANE HEENUM MENAD DAHRE LAM YAKUN SHAY-AM MAZKOORAA.\nSurely did come over Man to pass an occasion of time when he was nothing, mentioned of?\nاِنَّا خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ اَمْشَاجٍۖ نَّبْتَلِيْهِ فَجَعَلْنٰهُ سَمِيْعًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(2)\nINNAA KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN NUTFATIN AMSHAAZIN, NABTALEEHE FA-JA-A’LNAAHO SAMEE-A’M BASEERAA.\nVerily We created man from a (small insignificant) life drop of inter-mingled life germ (of both sexes); in order that We put him to trial, so We endowed him with hearing, seeing!\nاِنَّا هَدَيْنٰهُ السَّبِيْلَ اِمَّا شَاكِرًا وَّاِمَّا كَفُوْرًا‏(3)\nINNAA HADAYNAAHUS SABEELA IMMAA SHAAKERAWN WA IMMAA KAFOORAA.\nVerily, have We shown him the (Right) way, be he grateful or ungrateful!\nاِنَّاۤ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ سَلٰسِلَا۟ وَاَغْلٰلًا وَّسَعِيْرًا‏(4)\nINNAA A-A’TADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA SALAASELAA WA AGHLAALAWN WA SA-E’ERAA.\nVerily have We prepared for the disbelievers chains, and shackles and a flaming fire!\nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ يَشْرَبُوْنَ مِنْ كَاْسٍ كَانَ مِزَاجُهَا كَافُوْرًاۚ‏(5)\nINNAL ABRAARA YASHRABOONA MIN KA’SIN KAANA MEZAAJOHAA KAAFOORAA.\nVerily, the righteous ones shall drink of a cup tempered at the fountain ‘Kafoor’ (Camphor)!\nعَيْنًا يَّشْرَبُ بِهَا عِبَادُ اللّٰهِ يُفَجِّرُوْنَهَا تَفْجِيْرًا‏(6)\nA’YNAYN YASHRABO BEHAA E’BAADULLAAHE YOFAJJEROONAHAA TAFJEERAA.\nThe fountain whereof shall wherever drink the servants of God, they shall cause it to flow a desirable flow\nيُوْفُوْنَ بِالنَّذْرِ وَيَخَافُوْنَ يَوْمًا كَانَ شَرُّهٗ مُسْتَطِيْرًا‏(7)\nYOOFOONA BIN-NAZRE WA YAKHAAFOONA YAWMAN KAANA SARROHU MUSTA-TEERAA.\nThey who fulfil their vows, and fear the day the woe of which stretcheth far and wide\nوَيُطْعِمُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ عَلٰى حُبِّهٖ مِسْكِيْنًا وَّيَتِيْمًا وَّاَسِيْرًا‏(8)\nWA YUT-E’MUNAT TA-A’AMA A’LAA HUBBEHI MISKEENAWN WA YATEEMAWN WA ASEERAA.\nAnd (while needing it for themselves) they give away food, out of love for Him, to the poor and the orphan and the captive\nاِنَّمَا نُطْعِمُكُمْ لِوَجْهِ اللّٰهِ لَا نُرِيْدُ مِنْكُمْ جَزَآءً وَّلَا شُكُوْرًا‏(9)\nINNAMAA NUT-E’MOKUM LE WAJHIL LAAHE LAA NOREEDO MINKUM JA-ZAAA-AWN WA LAA SHOKOORAA.\n(Saying): “We feed you only for God’s sake, we intend not of you any recompense, nor (even) thanks (thereof)!\nاِنَّا نَخَافُ مِنْ رَّبِّنَا يَوْمًا عَبُوْسًا قَمْطَرِيْرًا‏(10)\nINNAA NAKHAAFO MIR RABBENAA YAWMAN A’BOOSAN QAMTAREERAA.\nVerily, we dread from our Lord, a stern day of distress\nفَوَقٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ شَرَّ ذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمِ وَ لَقّٰٮهُمْ نَضْرَةً وَّسُرُوْرًاۚ‏(11)\nFA-WAQAAHOMUL LAAHO SHARRA ZAALEKAL YAWME WA LAQQAAHUM NAZRATAWN WA SOROORAA.\nSo will God guard them from the evil of that day and cause them to meet freshness and pleasure\nوَجَزٰٮهُمْ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا جَنَّةً وَّحَرِيْرًا ۙ‏(12)\nWA JA-ZAAHUM BEMAA SABAROO JANNATAWN WA HAREERAM.\nAnd shall recompense them, for what they endured with patience, with garden (to abide) and silk (to wear)\nمُّتَّكِئِيْنَ فِيْهَا عَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِۚ لَا يَرَوْنَ فِيْهَا شَمْسًا وَّلَا زَمْهَرِيْرًاۚ‏(13)\nMUT-TAKE-EENA FEEHAA A’LAL A-RAAA-EK, LAA YARAWNA FEEHAA SHAMSAWN WA LAA ZAMHAREERAA.\nReclining therein on exalted couches, they shall find not therein (the excessive heat of) the sun, nor any (intense) cold\nوَدَانِيَةً عَلَيْهِمْ ظِلٰلُهَا وَذُلِّلَتْ قُطُوْفُهَا تَذْلِيْلًا‏(14)\nWA DAANEYATAN A’LAYHIM ZELAALOHAA WA ZULLAT QOTOOFOHAA TAZLEELAA.\nAnd close low over them (shall be) its shades, and the clustered fruits thereof (shall be) bowing down (in easy reach)\nوَيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِاٰنِيَةٍ مِّنْ فِضَّةٍ وَّاَكْوَابٍ كَانَتْ قَوَارِيْرَا۟ؔ ۙ‏(15)\nWA YOTAAFO A’LAYHIM BE-AANEYATIM MIN FIZZATIWN WA AKWAABIN KAANAT QAWAAREERAA.\nAnd shall pass round among them vessels of silver and goblets of crystal (glass)\nقَوَارِيْرَا۟ؔ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ قَدَّرُوْهَا تَقْدِيْرًا‏(16)\nQAWAAREERAA MIN FIZZATIN QADDAROOHAA TAQDEERAA.\nBright as glass, made of silver; measure they to a well-measure\nوَيُسْقَوْنَ فِيْهَا كَاْسًا كَانَ مِزَاجُهَا زَنْجَبِيْلًا ۚ‏(17)\nWA YUSQAWNA FEEHAA KA’SAN KAANA MEZAAJOHAA ZANJABEELAA.\nAnd they shall be supplied with the drink therein of a cup tempered with ‘Zanjabil’ (ginger)\nعَيْنًا فِيْهَا تُسَمّٰى سَلْسَبِيْلًا‏(18)\nA’YNAN FEEHAA TOSAMMAA SAL-SABEELAA.\n(It is the water of) a spring therein named ‘Salsabeel’ (The Soft Flowing)\nوَيَطُوْفُ عَلَيْهِمْ وِلْدَانٌ مُّخَلَّدُوْنَۚ اِذَا رَاَيْتَهُمْ حَسِبْتَهُمْ لُؤْلُؤًا مَّنْثُوْرًا‏(19)\nWA YATOOFO A’LAYHIM WILDAANUM MOKHALLADOON, EZAA RA-AYTAHUM HASIBTAHUM LO’LO-AM MANSOORAA.\nAnd around them in their service shall be boys (graced) with eternal youth; when thou seest them thou wilt deem them as pearls scattered about\nوَاِذَا رَاَيْتَ ثَمَّ رَاَيْتَ نَعِيْمًا وَّمُلْكًا كَبِيْرًا‏(20)\nWA EZAA RA-AYTA SUMMA RA-AYTA NA-E’EMAWN WA MULKAN KABEERAA.\nAnd when thou seest there, thou shalt see bounties (abundant) and a kingdom magnificent\nعٰلِيَهُمْ ثِيَابُ سُنْدُسٍ خُضْرٌ وَّاِسْتَبْرَقٌ وَّحُلُّوْۤا اَسَاوِرَ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ ۚوَسَقٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ شَرَابًا طَهُوْرًا‏(21)\nA’ALEYAHUM SEYAABO SUNDOSIN KHUZRUWN WA ISTABRAQUWN, WA HULLOO ASAAWERA MIN FIZZAH, WA SAQAAHUM RABBOHUM SHARAABAN TAHOORAA.\nUpon them shall be robes of fine green silk and rich brocade, and they shall be adorned with bracelets of silver, and their Lord give them to drink a drink, pure (and wholesome)\nاِنَّ هٰذَا كَانَ لَكُمْ جَزَآءً وَّكَانَ سَعْيُكُمْ مَّشْكُوْرًا‏(22)\nINNA HAAZAA KAANA LAKUM JA-ZAAA-AWN WA KAANA SA’YOKUM MASHKOORAA.\n(Saying unto them) “Verily this is unto you a recompense, and your endeavour is accepted (with appreciation)\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ تَنْزِيْلًا ۚ‏(23)\nINNAA NAHNO NAZZALNAA A’LAYKAL QURAANA TANZEELAA.\nVerily, We ourselves have sent down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) the Qur’an, in a proper descension\nفَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تُطِعْ مِنْهُمْ اٰثِمًا اَوْ كَفُوْرًاۚ‏(24)\nFASBIR LE HUKME RABBEKA WA LAA TO-TE’ MINHUM AASEMAN AW KAFOORAA.\nAwait then with patience the command of thy Lord, and obey not from among them a sinner or an ungrateful one\nوَاذْكُرِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ بُكْرَةً وَّاَصِيْلًا ۚ  ۖ‏(25)\nWAZKORISMA RABBEKA BUKRATAWN WA ASEELAA.\nAnd remember thou the name of thy Lord at morn and at even\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَاسْجُدْ لَهٗ وَسَبِّحْهُ لَيْلًا طَوِيْلًا‏(26)\nWA MENAL LAYLE FASJUD LAHU WA SABBEH-HO LAYLAN TAWEELAA.\nAnd during a part of the night prostrate thou in obeisance unto Him and celebrate His praise long night through\nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ يُحِبُّوْنَ الْعَاجِلَةَ وَيَذَرُوْنَ وَرَآءَهُمْ يَوْمًا ثَقِيْلًا‏(27)\nINNA HAA-O-LAAA-E YOHIBBOONAL A’AJELATA WA YAZAROONA WA RAAA-AHUM YAWMAN SAQEELAA.\nVerily, these (people) love the fleeting present, and (neglect) putting away behind them the Day (which shall be) hard\nنَحْنُ خَلَقْنٰهُمْ وَشَدَدْنَاۤ اَسْرَهُمْۚ وَاِذَا شِئْنَا بَدَّلْنَاۤ اَمْثَالَهُمْ تَبْدِيْلًا‏(28)\nNAHNO KHALAQNAAHUM WA SHADADNAA ASRAHUM, WA EZAA SHE’NAA BAD-DALNAA AMSAALAHUM TABDEELAA.\nWe Ourselves created them and made them strong in their parts, and when We will, with the like of them, will We replace them\nاِنَّ هٰذِهٖ تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ فَمَنْ شَآءَ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ سَبِيْلًا‏(29)\nINNA HAAZEHI TAZKERAH, FAMAN SHAAA-AT TAKHAZA ELAA RABBEHI SABEELAA.\nVerily this is a Reminder, so whosoever pleaseth, taketh unto his Lord the (Right) way\nوَمَا تَشَآءُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا  ۖ‏(30)\nWAMAA TA-SHAAA-OONA ILLAA AYN YA-SHAAA-ALLAAH, INNALLAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAYN.\nAnd ye desire not save what God desireth; Verily God is All-Knowing, the All-Wise\nيُّدْخِلُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖؕ وَالظّٰلِمِيْنَ اَعَدَّ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا‏(31)\nYUDKHELO MAYN YA-SHAAA-O FEE RAHMATEH, WAZ ZAALEMEENA A-A’DDA LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nHe admitteth whosoever He willeth into His mercy; and (as for) the unjust ones, He hath prepared for them a painful chastisement",
  "merits": "Surah al-Dahr (The Period)\nThis Surah is also called al-Insaan (The Man). It was revealed in Makkah and it has 31 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.w.t.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is Jannah and its bounties.\nIf a person recites this Surah, especially on Thursday mornings, he will be rewarded with a hundred houries and four thousand slaves in Jannah and he will be given a place close to that of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). Reciting it win war brings victory. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is good for those with heart problems."
